<TrustPage
  title="How we use AI"
  description="Which AI tools GeurtsGaming uses, what we use them for, and what they never do."
  heading="How we use AI"
  lede="We use AI tools to help us make things. This page says which ones, what for, and where a person stays in charge."
>
  <div class="summary">
    <h2>The short version</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>AI helps us build.</strong> We use it to help write code, make some artwork and draft some of the words on this site.</li>
      <li><strong>People decide.</strong> A person reads, tests and approves what goes live.</li>
      <li><strong>No AI in the arcade demo.</strong> The demo on this site does not use AI while you play.</li>
      <li><strong>One of our games does.</strong> In Cool Typing Games, the computer players' chat is written by AI.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <h2>What we use AI for</h2>

  <h3>Writing code</h3>
  <p>
    We write and test code with the help of AI coding assistants: Claude, made by Anthropic, and Antigravity,
    made by Google. They suggest and write code and run tests. We review what they produce and decide what ships.
  </p>

  <h3>Artwork and logos</h3>
  <p>Some of our artwork and logos are made with the help of AI tools. A person chooses them and finishes them.</p>

  <h3>The words on this site</h3>
  <p>Some of the text on this site, including these pages, was drafted with AI and then checked and edited by us.</p>

  <h2>AI inside our games</h2>

  <h3>The arcade demo on this site</h3>
  <p>The demo does not use AI while you play:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>The sums and typing lines are made by ordinary code following fixed rules.</li>
    <li>The voices are the ones built in to your own device. Nothing is sent to an AI service to make them.</li>
    <li>The wingman that flies beside you when nobody else is online is a simple scripted ship.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Cool Typing Games</h3>
  <p>
    Cool Typing Games has computer-controlled players, and they can chat. Their messages are written by an AI
    model from OpenAI. So that a computer player can answer sensibly, the game sends the model the recent chat
    from that match, which includes players' usernames and what they typed. The model is told to stay in
    character and not to use offensive language.
  </p>

  <h2>What AI does not do here</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>It does not decide anything about a child: not their score, their grade or what they are allowed to do.</li>
    <li>It does not talk to anyone in the arcade demo on this site.</li>
    <li>It is not given personal information by this site, because this site does not collect any. See the <a href="/privacy/">privacy page</a>.</li>
  </ul>
</TrustPage>
